\section{Discussion and Limitations}
The numerical solution approximates the exact flow up to truncation and
round-off error. For chaotic systems, individual trajectories are only
meaningful over a finite predictability horizon set by the largest Lyapunov
exponent; statistical and geometric properties (attractor shape, invariant
measures) remain robust. Spatial discretisation, finite precision and the
chosen step size all bound the fidelity of the results.

